Live 0.5.0 two-device proof — real Hermes 0.22.5, plugin built from
committed HEAD 102a685 on main (merge of the 0.4.2 first-pull config fixes
and feat/multi-profile), local BARE GIT remote.

Homes (scratch, deleted after the run):
  A = <work>/roam-homes/v5-a   (device vps)   — default home + REAL
      `hermes profile create` profiles work and personal, each with its own
      SOUL, memory, skill and config, and one REAL ended session per home
      (root, work, personal) imported with Hermes's own
      `hermes sessions import --from claude` and end-stamped; sync_sessions on
  B = <work>/roam-homes/v5-b   (device beta) — brand-new device
Shared store: <work>/roam-homes/v5-remote.git (bare git remote)
Fleet archive key: generated per `hermes roam init`'s instructions, written
to both homes' .env (and hand-provisioned into B's profiles/work/.env),
never printed.

Every command ran as
  cd <work> && HERMES_HOME=<home> hermes ...

Verified end to end (assertions in the driver, exit 0):
  1. A's push names the covered root with all three profiles' sync state and
     publishes 3 session transcripts (default, work, personal).
  2. B's plan-only pull shows the brand-new-device notice and the covered
     root; the apply keeps the conflicts local; --overwrite-conflicts takes
     the remote home wholesale.
  3. Both profiles are listable on B with their soul and skill; the root
     SOUL and memory arrived.
  4. The first-pull config union brought the shared model keys into B's root
     config AND both pulled profile configs while B's own api_key and theme
     stayed; A's api_keys never travelled.
  5. `hermes roam sessions` on B groups the archive vps/default,
     vps/work and vps/personal; `sessions show` prints one transcript with
     the read-only note.
  6. `hermes -p work roam status` on B reports the ROOT home (not the
     profile home) and the covered root.
  7. A stale push on B is refused with exit code 2; pulling converges the
     fleet; `hermes roam doctor` passes 10/10 on both homes.

